# Positioning the Legend Inside the Plot

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Section

Use `layout.legend` with `x`, `y`, `xanchor`, and `yanchor` (paper coords,
0–1) to place the legend inside the plot area.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

Figure.new()
|> Figure.add_trace(Scatter.new(x: [1, 2, 3], y: [2, 1, 3], name: "A", mode: "lines"))
|> Figure.add_trace(Scatter.new(x: [1, 2, 3], y: [3, 2, 1], name: "B", mode: "lines"))
|> Figure.update_layout(
  title: "Legend Inside the Plot (top-right)",
  legend: %{x: 1, xanchor: "right", y: 1}
)
|> Plotly.show()
```
